  "problem": "A statistician collected data on the height above the ground (in hundreds of meters) of a hot air balloon during the first five minutes of its flight. This data is shown below. \n\n| Time $(x)$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Height $(y)$ | $1.6$ | $3.0$ | $4.6$ | $6$ | $7.6$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the balloon's height after $6$ minutes, assuming the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}22.8 \\\\ 83.4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*",
